WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:04.397
<v Examiner>Semen, sperm count, erection and ejaculation.

2
00:00:04.847 --> 00:00:10.578
<v Examiner>Describe the composition of semen, and the normal sperm count in relation to sterility.

3
00:00:10.578 --> 00:00:14.333
<v Examiner>Then describe the physiology of the male sexual response,

4
00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:16.836
<v Examiner>and relate it to erectile dysfunction.

5
00:00:17.286 --> 00:00:18.558
Two checklist points.

6
00:00:18.558 --> 00:00:21.588
Her quizzes ask the semen part as match-the-gland,

7
00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.497
and the erection part as put-the-steps-in-order.

8
00:00:24.947 --> 00:00:27.435
The hook for semen: sixty, thirty, ten.

9
00:00:27.435 --> 00:00:31.710
Sixty per cent from the seminal vesicles, thirty from the prostate,

10
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.750
and ten from everything else: the sperm themselves, the testes, the epididymis,

11
00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.600
and the bulbourethral glands.

12
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.497
Semen is a milky, sticky mixture of sperm and the accessory gland fluids.

13
00:00:43.497 --> 00:00:46.481
It gives the sperm a transport medium; nutrients,

14
00:00:46.481 --> 00:00:51.172
fructose from the seminal vesicles and citrate from the prostate; protection;

15
00:00:51.172 --> 00:00:52.512
and it activates them.

16
00:00:52.512 --> 00:00:57.385
It's alkaline, which neutralises the acid in the male urethra and in the vagina.

17
00:00:57.385 --> 00:01:00.309
Its prostaglandins thin the mucus in the cervix,

18
00:01:00.309 --> 00:01:05.303
and set off reverse peristalsis in the uterus, which helps the sperm on their way.

19
00:01:05.303 --> 00:01:10.725
Clotting factors make it sticky straight after ejaculation, then an enzyme, fibrinolysin,

20
00:01:10.725 --> 00:01:11.882
liquefies it again.

21
00:01:12.332 --> 00:01:12.970
The count.

22
00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.713
Only two to five millilitres is ejaculated,

23
00:01:15.713 --> 00:01:20.626
but it holds fifty to a hundred and thirty million sperm in every millilitre.

24
00:01:20.626 --> 00:01:26.049
Her quiz key: as many as seven hundred and fifty million sperm can be released in one

25
00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:26.814
ejaculation.

26
00:01:26.814 --> 00:01:29.047
Sterility is linked to a low count:

27
00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:32.684
below about twenty to twenty-five million per millilitre.

28
00:01:34.134 --> 00:01:36.072
Now the male sexual response.

29
00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:37.809
The hook: point and shoot.

30
00:01:37.809 --> 00:01:42.219
Parasympathetic for the erection, sympathetic for the ejaculation.

31
00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:43.235
Erection.

32
00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:48.641
Sexual arousal sets off a parasympathetic reflex, which releases nitric oxide locally.

33
00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:52.350
Nitric oxide relaxes the smooth muscle in the vessel walls,

34
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:56.499
so the arterioles dilate and the erectile tissue fills with blood.

35
00:01:56.499 --> 00:02:01.151
The corpora cavernosa expand, and that squashes the veins that drain them,

36
00:02:01.151 --> 00:02:02.534
so the blood stays in.

37
00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:05.363
The corpus spongiosum keeps the urethra open.

38
00:02:05.363 --> 00:02:09.827
An erection can be started, or stopped, by thoughts and emotions alone.

39
00:02:10.277 --> 00:02:11.057
Ejaculation.

40
00:02:11.057 --> 00:02:16.650
Sympathetic nerves make the ducts and the accessory glands contract and empty into the

41
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.170
urethra.

42
00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.487
The bladder sphincter closes, so no urine gets out.

43
00:02:20.487 --> 00:02:23.998
And the bulbospongiosus muscles contract rhythmically,

44
00:02:23.998 --> 00:02:26.405
pumping the semen out of the urethra.

45
00:02:26.855 --> 00:02:32.417
Erectile dysfunction, or impotence, is the inability to attain an erection.

46
00:02:32.417 --> 00:02:38.202
Her slide adds how Viagra works: an enzyme called P D E 5 breaks down c G M P,

47
00:02:38.202 --> 00:02:43.987
the messenger that keeps the smooth muscle relaxed, and Viagra blocks P D E 5.

48
00:02:43.987 --> 00:02:45.841
So the vessels stay open.

49
00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:46.890
<v Examiner>Once more.

50
00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.043
<v Examiner>Semen, and the male sexual response.

51
00:02:51.493 --> 00:02:56.063
Semen is sixty per cent from the seminal vesicles, thirty from the prostate,

52
00:02:56.063 --> 00:02:58.228
and ten from the sperm and the rest.

53
00:02:58.228 --> 00:03:02.497
It carries, feeds, protects and activates the sperm, and it's alkaline.

54
00:03:02.497 --> 00:03:07.848
Two to five millilitres holds fifty to a hundred and thirty million sperm per millilitre,

55
00:03:07.848 --> 00:03:11.576
and a count below about twenty million is linked to sterility.

56
00:03:11.576 --> 00:03:15.484
Erection is parasympathetic: nitric oxide dilates the arterioles,

57
00:03:15.484 --> 00:03:19.092
the corpora cavernosa fill, and the veins are squashed shut.

58
00:03:19.092 --> 00:03:23.722
Ejaculation is sympathetic: the ducts contract, the bladder sphincter closes,

59
00:03:23.722 --> 00:03:26.367
and the bulbospongiosus pumps the semen out.

60
00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:29.915
Erectile dysfunction is being unable to attain an erection.
